%% Sequence 02c — Delete task
%% Updated: 2026-07-28.
%% Scenario: an authorized task deleter soft-deletes an eligible task.
%% Evidence status: Implemented; current User-realm policy permits task creator, Organization owner/admin, and ProjectRole.MEMBER; System Admin is a separate realm and is not part of this policy. Hard delete is a separate restricted option.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor PM as Authorized task deleter
    participant B as «boundary» Browser
    participant C as «boundary» DeleteTaskController
    participant K as «control» DeleteTaskCommand
    participant D as «entity» PostgreSQL
    participant E as «control» TaskEventPublisher
    participant N as «control» NotificationCreator

    Note over PM,K: Current canDeleteTask policy does not grant deletion from ProjectRole.OWNER or MANAGER alone

    PM->>B: Confirm task deletion
    activate B
    B->>C: DELETE /tasks/:taskId
    activate C
    C->>K: execute(DeleteTaskDTO)
    activate K
    K->>D: Lock task, check permission, hours and review debt
    activate D
    D-->>K: Task and blocking records
    deactivate D
    alt Eligible for deletion
        K->>D: Set deleted_at and write audit
        activate D
        D-->>K: Committed
        deactivate D
        K->>E: publishTaskDeleted(event)
        activate E
        E-->>K: Published
        deactivate E
        K->>N: Notify assignee/creator when applicable
        activate N
        N-->>K: Notifications handled
        deactivate N
        K-->>C: Success result
    else Blocked by policy/work/review evidence
        K-->>C: Failure result with reason
    end
    deactivate K
    C-->>B: Redirect/result
    deactivate C
    B-->>PM: Refresh canonical Project board or show error
    deactivate B
